  "summary": "I added a \"Close portal\" button below the canvas in `src/main.ts`. Clicking it hides the energy disc, the core glow and all three particle groups, and stops the particle simulation. It sets `window.__TASK_STATE__` to `portalActive: false` and `particleCount: 0`, and changes the label to \"Open portal\". The three portal point lights fade out over about half a second. Clicking again shows the nodes, restarts the particle pools and restores the label and `portalActive: true`. `particleCount` goes back to the live particle count on the next frame, because the loop overwrites the state each frame. Clicks are ignored until `app.ready()` resolves.\n\nTypecheck passes and the render shows no errors, with the button below the canvas and the portal drawn normally in its open state. I did not click the button or confirm the closed state, so that behaviour is untested."
}